{"title":"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Carolyn has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> bill, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af88c1534bab510152766fb60851db0c3a5af52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> bill, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555360df10d7f3448442d43c277f763b0d1236bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> bill, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94b4cab8f57e8d3121cd9bb4de67feb31a48a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> bill in her wallet. She closes her eyes and removes one of the four bills from her wallet. What is the probability that the total value of the three bills left in her wallet is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea40cf0e9e3563a6ea210a10440532140fc55826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e365d9b4c3af9b9cd6bce4e1f30a36536cb34cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 0.25 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0.75 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"412\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can look at different cases for the dollar bill that was removed, and then see what the sum would be. We also know that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> total possibilities of dollar bills that she can remove.\n</p><p>First, if Carolyn removes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill, the total value remaining would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b5a36dcd83e45d6b5a510e2cf8ce8526c2decc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 20 + 50 = 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />. This is more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can also conclude that removing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill would also result in a total value greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from this because the value of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill is less than the value of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill, so adding the remaining values will result in a value larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Second, if Carolyn removes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill, the total value remaining would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202c4d0fc4b10409d24bccd367eb5daed15b2b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 10 + 50 = 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />. This is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can also conclude that removing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollar bill would also result in a total value less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> using similar logic.\n</p><p>Of the possibilities above, we can see that there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> where the total value was greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the probability is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfba1940af6e344537849eb143d19e1976f7644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{2 \\times 25}{4 \\times 25} = \\frac{50}{100} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 0.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"243\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"